&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Workato&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;Workato is the leading Control and Execution Platform for Enterprise AI — the neutral platform enterprises trust to put AI to work across their business. Workato unifies data, applications, and processes into a single platform so AI can reliably orchestrate business processes in production at enterprise scale. Built on more than a decade of running mission-critical processes for over half the Fortune 500 — including Nasdaq, Amazon, Cisco, Vodafone, Atlassian, and Lucid Motors — Workato turns over 14,000 enterprise systems AI needs to act on into one governed execution layer. For more information, visit &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.workato.com/&quot; data-tooltip-link-label=&quot;undefined&quot;&gt;workato.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;Ultimately, Workato believes in fostering a &lt;strong&gt;flexible, trust-oriented culture that empowers everyone to take full ownership of their roles&lt;/strong&gt;. We are driven by &lt;strong&gt;innovation &lt;/strong&gt;and looking for&lt;strong&gt; team players &lt;/strong&gt;who want to actively build our company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;But, we also believe in &lt;strong&gt;balancing productivity with self-care&lt;/strong&gt;. That’s why we offer all of our employees a vibrant and dynamic work environment &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot; href=&quot;http://www.workato.com/careers&quot;&gt;along with a multitude of benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; they can enjoy inside and outside of their work lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;If this sounds right up your alley, please submit an application. We look forward to getting to know you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;Also, feel free to check out why:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.businessinsider.com/47-enterprise-startups-to-bet-your-career-on-in-2020-2019-12&quot;&gt;Business Insider&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; named us an “enterprise startup to bet your career on”&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot; href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/cloud100/#a57477b5f941&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Cloud 100&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; recognized us as one of the top 100 private cloud companies in the world&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot; href=&quot;https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/pages/technology-media-and-telecommunications/articles/fast500-winners.html&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot;&gt;Deloitte Tech Fast 500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ranked us as the 17th fastest growing tech company in the Bay Area, and 96th in North America&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(8, 55, 99);&quot; href=&quot;https://qz.com/work/2053446/the-best-companies-for-working-from-home/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 212, 216);&quot;&gt;Quartz&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ranked us the #1 best company for remote workers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We seek an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Senior Go Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join the Workato Genie team. In this role, you will be responsible for developing mission-critical features and services for the Workato platform, including AI chatbot dispatching and balancing synchronous and asynchronous AI execution. In this role, y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;ou will also be responsible to:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build high-performance gateways and routing components&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build server-side infrastructure for logging and monitoring&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work closely with Infra and SRE teams to ensure high availability and scalability requirements are addressed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate closely with the AI team to design and implement innovative features for a new AI assistant, ensuring cutting-edge performance and user experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute at all phases of the development lifecycle&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Write well-designed, testable, efficient code&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate and propose improvements to the existing system&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support continuous improvement by investigating alternatives and technologies and presenting these for architectural review&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications / Experience / Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BS/MS degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related subject&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;8+ years of industry experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience with Go language at backend (4+ years)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent debugging, analytical, problem-solving, and social skills&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good understanding of all building blocks of large web applications: databases, load balancers, application servers, message brokers, caching, monitoring, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with building and scaling distributed, highly available systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in Ruby on Rails is a plus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contributions to open-source projects are a big plus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understanding of possible bottlenecks in a code and a solution in general&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least basic knowledge of Kubernetes concepts and configuration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Docker and other isolation technologies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Redis-based caching&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with public cloud infrastructure providers (AWS/Azure/Google Cloud)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in related fields (DevOps, ML, DBA, Enterprise applications, etc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with third-party REST APIs at scale (request throttling, batch processing, etc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills / Personal Characteristics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Readiness to work remotely with teams distributed across the world and timezones&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spoken English (at a level enough to pass technical interviews and work with colleagues)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open to new technologies and willing to experiment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-cycle product feature delivery mindset (from design to production and maintenance).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(REQ ID: 2941)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Orcrist is building a next generation data intelligence platform using cutting-edge technologies. We&#39;re handling petabyte-scale data with sub-second queries. Our product is a Kubernetes‑based platform delivered as B2B SaaS or as a self‑hosted on‑prem solution, including air‑gapped deployments. We enable customers across defense, law enforcement, and enterprise to turn mission-critical data into actionable intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Every investigation starts with data. As PM for the Integration team, you make sure analysts in law enforcement and defense have the data they need, when they need it. You own the roadmap for integrating data from commercial vendors, open feeds, social media and messaging platforms, as well as the admin interfaces used to manage these integrations. Your work ensures data arrives current, traceable to its source and ready to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a largely technical PM role with significant ownership over a platform and admin experience that are still taking shape. You decide what gets built and in what order, working closely with engineers and other product teams to turn provider APIs and data models into scalable integrations and features that support analysts’ investigations. You’ll read API documentation, map provider data to OIP’s data model and write clear, actionable specs that engineers can build from.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the provider roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt; We add a source when it answers a question analysts can’t answer today, so you start from the analyst’s problem, not from a provider’s name. You talk regularly with analysts, admins and solutions engineers in law enforcement and defense, and with the upstream teams whose features bring integration requests. You decide which providers come next and what “done” means for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write the technical specs.&lt;/strong&gt; Cover authentication, pagination, rate limits and quotas, incremental sync, deduplication, field mapping, and how failures surface. Every object must carry its provider, fetch time and source URL from the moment it is fetched. Our platform runs as SaaS and on-prem, so you also decide how each source behaves in each distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the connectors as a product.&lt;/strong&gt; That covers the contract between connectors and the platform, versioning, and how quickly a new provider goes from evaluation to production. Every connector should make the next one cheaper. Where another team can reach a public source on its own, you give it a safe way to do so instead of putting it in our queue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the admin interfaces.&lt;/strong&gt; That means creating a connection, managing credentials, scheduling, health and status, logs, quota usage and permissions. A source we can’t monitor isn’t delivered, so every live connection needs a health check and clear failure states.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with partnerships and legal.&lt;/strong&gt; You collaborate with the Director of OSINT and the Data Acquisition Manager to evaluate vendors, raise licensing and terms-of-service questions before we build, and turn the legal framework (storage, retention, redistribution) into product requirements. You also give the people negotiating contracts technical findings and cost per call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the teams around you.&lt;/strong&gt; Upstream, you work with the teams building user-facing features, such as graphs and maps, who bring integration requests from their intelligence domain. You help them find the analyst question behind each request and decide whether a shared connector can serve several of them. Downstream, you work with the foundation teams for ontology, machine learning and processing, so incoming data arrives in a shape they can use. You forecast the load of every high-volume source before it goes live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape person-focused investigation tools.&lt;/strong&gt; You own how analysts go from a first lead about a person to a reviewed set of linked online identities. That includes how results are presented and reviewed, and how to avoid paying for the same lookup twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure the integration layer.&lt;/strong&gt; Track sync success rate, data freshness, time to onboard a provider, active connections, and time to resolve a failed connection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years as a Product Manager in B2B SaaS, with experience owning a technically complex area end-to-end, such as an integration platform, an API product, or data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable in API documentation. You can discuss OAuth versus API keys, polling versus webhooks, pagination and rate limits with engineers as an equal, and you can try an endpoint yourself in Postman or curl.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have designed admin or configuration interfaces for technical users: connection setup, status and error states, audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write specs and acceptance criteria that are specific enough to build and test against.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are data-fluent and define quality metrics for reliability and coverage, not just feature delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with the legal side of third-party data: licensing, terms of service, GDPR, and provenance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well across teams, since integrations touch engineering, partnerships, customer success, and every product that consumes the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to work in Germany and willing to travel to Berlin and across DACH for workshops and customer visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built or managed a connector framework, integration marketplace, or iPaaS product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with OSINT as a practitioner or product builder, and a sense of where existing collection tools fall short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Kubernetes, on-prem, or air-gapped deployment constraints and what they mean for integration architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with entity resolution or link analysis, and how ingested data feeds them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language (B1+)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with law enforcement or defense users in Germany or the DACH region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 [&amp;quot;list&amp;quot;,{&amp;quot;spread&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;start&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;end&amp;quot;:273},&amp;quot;regular_list_item&amp;quot;,{&amp;quot;start&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;end&amp;quot;:273}]&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real ownership, real impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Own a critical layer of the platform that every customer relies on. Much of the integration platform and its admin experience is still taking shape, so you identify the problems, set priorities, decide what gets built, and see it through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first, Germany-wide: &lt;/strong&gt;Work from wherever you do your best work, with regular team gatherings in Berlin and other off-site locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility by default: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible working hours help you make work fit your life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your setup, your way: &lt;/strong&gt;Get a personal home-office equipment budget to create a workspace that works for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 days of vacation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Take the time you need to recharge and come back with fresh energy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep growing: &lt;/strong&gt;We invest in your personal and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get rewarded for impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Performance bonuses are tied to agreed objectives and key results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A warm welcome: &lt;/strong&gt;Every new team member gets a welcome goodie bag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good people, good times: &lt;/strong&gt;From summer and Christmas parties to regular team gatherings, we make time to celebrate together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A mission that matters: &lt;/strong&gt;Work on challenges with tangible impact on public safety and national security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Orcrist is building a next generation data intelligence platform using cutting-edge technologies. We&#39;re handling petabyte-scale data with sub-second queries. Our product is a Kubernetes‑based platform delivered as B2B SaaS or as a self‑hosted on‑prem solution, including air‑gapped deployments. We enable customers across defense, law enforcement, and enterprise to turn mission-critical data into actionable intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;As Data Protection &amp;amp; Quality Management Officer at Orcrist Technologies, you own our data protection framework and build and operate our ISO 9001 quality management system. You act as our appointed Data Protection Officer under GDPR and lead the development, maintenance, and continuous improvement of our QMS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Both are independent staff functions reporting directly to the C-Level Management. You advise, monitor, audit, and document; the business remains responsible for operational decisions and implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build AI platforms for customers in the defence and government sector. Data protection and quality management are essential to our business and customer trust. As the company grows, you will build these structures hands-on, working closely with engineering, product, people, IT, and our Information Security Officer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain our data protection management system, including policies, processes, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as our appointed DPO under Art. 37–39 GDPR and § 38 BDSG, advising management and teams on GDPR, BDSG, and TDDDG requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor compliance, including records of processing activities, processor agreements, TOMs, data protection impact assessments, and data subject requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on privacy by design, international data transfers, retention, and personal data breaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain our ISO 9001 QMS, including process documentation, quality objectives, risk-based thinking, and continual improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the internal audit programme, track nonconformities and corrective actions, and coordinate certification and surveillance audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the annual management review and report on data protection risks, audit findings, and improvement priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train teams on data protection and quality management requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the ISB to align overlapping requirements while maintaining clear responsibilities and independence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel occasionally to our offices in Berlin, Dresden, and Hamburg, as well as to other workshop locations across Germany, to facilitate workshops, training sessions, and audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-site presence is expected to be more frequent during the initial implementation phase and primarily driven by audits and specific business needs thereafter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified DPO training (GDD, TÜV, DEKRA, or equivalent) and at least 3 years of hands-on GDPR experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 years of practical ISO 9001 experience and an internal auditor qualification based on ISO 19011.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining data protection management systems and QMS documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The independence to challenge management, the judgement to prioritise risks, and a pragmatic approach to implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on mindset and confidence working with technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel occasionally within Germany and work in a hybrid setup, combining remote work with on-site activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German and English at C1 level or above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a software, SaaS, or AI company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ISO/IEC 27001.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AQAP-Standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CIPP/E or comparable certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a first ISO 9001 certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GRC platforms or document control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first, Germany-wide:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Work from wherever you do your best work, with regular team gatherings in Berlin and other off-site locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility by default: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible working hours help you make work fit your life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your setup, your way: &lt;/strong&gt;Get a personal home-office equipment budget to create a workspace that works for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 days of vacation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Take the time you need to recharge and come back with fresh energy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep growing: &lt;/strong&gt;We invest in your personal and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get rewarded for impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Performance bonuses are tied to agreed objectives and key results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A warm welcome: &lt;/strong&gt;Every new team member gets a welcome goodie bag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good people, good times: &lt;/strong&gt;From summer and Christmas parties to regular team gatherings, we make time to celebrate together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A mission that matters: &lt;/strong&gt;Work on challenges with tangible impact on public safety and national security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About commercetools&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real innovation starts with a strong foundation, and at commercetools, that comes from the perfect balance of our product and our people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Behind every leap forward is a collective of builders, explorers, doers, makers, and problem-solvers. The kind of people who not only created composable commerce but also shaped the culture of experimentation that idea unlocked. Together they are the engine of commerce innovation today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At commercetools, we power the next era of commerce for our customers. Whether it’s AI-driven solutions that help enterprises make smarter business decisions, bridging digital and physical shopping experiences, or enabling entirely new ways for industries to connect with their customers, we help the world’s most ambitious companies experiment, scale, and grow without limits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here the best idea wins, not the loudest voice. You will have the tools, trust, and space to not only build the future of commerce, but to build your own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Über unser Customer Success Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hallo! Ich bin &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/enricocellini/&quot;&gt;Enrico&lt;/a&gt;, Customer Success Team Lead bei commercetools. Mein Team konzentriert sich auf den Aufbau langfristiger, beratungsorientierter Partnerschaften mit unseren Enterprise-Kunden.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unser Customer Success Team gestaltet und skaliert mit Leidenschaft eine außergewöhnliche Upmarket Customer Experience im gesamten Enterprise-Segment. Im Zuge unseres weiteren Wachstums freuen wir uns darauf, unser Team in EMEA um eine:n &lt;strong&gt;Senior Customer Success Manager (m/w/d)&lt;/strong&gt; zu erweitern.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In dieser Rolle bilden Sie das entscheidende Bindeglied zwischen unseren Kunden und den modernsten Commerce-Produkten auf dem Markt. Sie betreuen unsere größten und komplexesten Enterprise-Kunden – von schnell wachsenden Marken bis hin zu börsennotierten Unternehmen. Dabei konzentrieren Sie sich auf Account Health, die Post-Sales-Adoption und die Positionierung von commercetools als vertrauenswürdigen strategischen Partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sie arbeiten eng mit unseren internen Support-, Produkt- und Vertriebsteams zusammen, um optimale Voraussetzungen für den Erfolg unserer Kunden zu schaffen. Da commercetools leistungsstark, modern und hochgradig flexibel ist, setzen Sie Ihr tiefes technisches Verständnis, Ihre Vertriebsaffinität und Ihre erstklassigen Kommunikationsfähigkeiten ein, um große Marken bei der Gestaltung außergewöhnlicher Commerce-Workflows zu unterstützen und langfristigen Mehrwert zu schaffen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Über das Account Management hinaus tragen Sie aktiv dazu bei, unsere Customer-Success-Praxis sowohl regional als auch global mitzugestalten und weiterzuentwickeln.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wenn Sie bereit sind, innovative Lösungen für bekannte Marken voranzutreiben, die Kundenkommunikation über verschiedene Kanäle hinweg zu steuern und in einer einflussreichen Rolle aufzublühen, freuen wir uns darauf, Sie kennenzulernen!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Der Interviewprozess für diese Position findet auf Englisch statt. Wir suchen daher eine Person, die sowohl auf Deutsch als auch auf Englisch sicher mit unseren Kunden kommunizieren kann.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ihre Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie begleiten Enterprise-Kunden dabei, den Mehrwert unserer Agentic-Commerce-Architektur – einschließlich Composable Commerce, Frontend und Connect – zu maximieren und flexible, zukunftssichere Tech-Stacks aufzubauen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie übersetzen neue Produktfeatures und -funktionen in klare Geschäftsergebnisse und stimmen diese direkt auf die strategischen Ziele und zentralen ROI-Kennzahlen des jeweiligen Kunden ab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie treiben Kundenbeziehungen proaktiv voran und leiten wirkungsvolle Strategic Business Reviews (SBRs), um die Kundenbindung zu stärken, die Plattformnutzung zu steigern und langfristiges Wachstum zu beschleunigen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie arbeiten eng mit dem Produktmanagement zusammen, vertreten die Bedürfnisse unserer Kunden und liefern entscheidendes Feedback, das die Roadmap unserer neuesten Produktinnovationen mitgestaltet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie arbeiten nahtlos und teamübergreifend mit Sales, Product und Support zusammen, bringen tiefgehendes technisches und kaufmännisches Know-how ein und sichern so langfristig den Erfolg unserer Enterprise-Kunden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie repräsentieren commercetools in Webinaren, Kundenfallstudien und Beratungsgremien, um Kundenerfolge sichtbar zu machen und das Engagement innerhalb der Community zu fördern.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie übernehmen eine zentrale Rolle bei der Weiterentwicklung globaler Customer-Success-Frameworks, treiben interne Prozessverbesserungen voran und gestalten die langfristige operative Strategie der Abteilung mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie agieren intern und extern als anerkannte:r Fachexpert:in, unterstützen Teammitglieder als Mentor:in, fördern die funktionsübergreifende Zusammenarbeit und tragen dazu bei, die gemeinsamen Standards unserer Customer-Success-Praxis weiter anzuheben.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie fungieren als Eskalationsinstanz und arbeiten mit dem Product-Support-Team zusammen, um Probleme schnell zu lösen. Auch in anspruchsvollen Eskalationssituationen bleiben Sie ruhig, professionell und besonnen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Was Sie mitbringen – Ihr Profil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindestens fünf Jahre Erfahrung in einem High-Touch-Tech-Umfeld mit nachweisbaren Erfolgen im Bereich Customer Success, Pre-Sales oder Technical Consulting – idealerweise in den Branchen E-Commerce oder Retail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deutschkenntnisse auf muttersprachlichem Niveau sowie verhandlungssichere Englischkenntnisse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ein tiefes technisches Verständnis moderner API-first- und Headless-Technologien, gepaart mit betriebswirtschaftlichem Denken und der Fähigkeit, komplexe Technologien in messbaren ROI zu übersetzen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Die Fähigkeit, als überzeugende:r und vertrauenswürdige:r Berater:in aufzutreten, Gespräche auf C-Level-Ebene zu führen, Kundenstrategien mitzugestalten und Expansionspotenziale sicher zu identifizieren und zu erschließen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine strukturierte und agile Arbeitsweise sowie die Fähigkeit, komplexe Accounts über globale, funktionsübergreifende Teams hinweg eigenverantwortlich zu betreuen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine teamorientierte Persönlichkeit, die in einer dynamischen, internationalen Tech-Kultur aufblüht, sowie eine Reisebereitschaft von bis zu 50 %, um wertvolle Kundenbeziehungen aufzubauen und zu pflegen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Von Vorteil:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weitere Sprachkenntnisse (Französisch oder Spanisch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because work and life are connected, our benefits are too. We’ve designed them to give you the security, flexibility, and opportunities you need to focus on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🩺 &lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive health benefits&lt;/strong&gt; for you and your dependents, including access to OpenUp for personalized mental health support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 &lt;strong&gt;Learning and development &lt;/strong&gt;opportunities including an annual learning budget, access to self-paced learning platforms and language training, personalized coaching, mentorship, and leadership programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼 &lt;strong&gt;Family Leave Plus&lt;/strong&gt; gives you additional fully paid weeks of parental leave on top of government-provided leave, so you can spend more time with your new addition&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 &lt;strong&gt;Our equity participation program&lt;/strong&gt; allows you to share in our success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on our benefits, &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/careers/our-benefits&quot;&gt;visit this page.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come as you are. Build with us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your unique perspective is essential to our success. We are committed to building a team that reflects the world around us because we know it’s the only way to build the future. We celebrate our differences and have created a hiring process that’s fair, inclusive, and designed to let your talent shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We proudly welcome applicants of every race, color, religion, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, and any other part of your identity that makes you who you are. As an equal opportunity employer, we believe that our strength lies in our diversity, and we invite you to be a part of our global community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on our diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging practices, &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/careers/dei-esg&quot;&gt;visit this page&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

