&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected Operations™ Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing — and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Working at Samsara means you’ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that’s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you’ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is a fortress in a volatile market. We are a $1.9B ARR, NYSE-listed powerhouse that sells essential technology to the physical operations powering the global economy. This is a seat built for high performers and incredibly driven individuals who want to accelerate their careers — the bar for entry is high, but those who execute are well rewarded for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While the rest of the tech scene is scaling back, our France team continued to perform above 100% last year. We are looking for territory owners who want to manage deal cycles from €&lt;strong&gt;20k to &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;€&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;200k&lt;/strong&gt;, selling a complex suite of 15+ products to 8 different personas, including MDs and Finance Directors. If you want to be pushed to your limit and rewarded with the stability of a market leader, this is the place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whilst the role can be worked remotely anywhere in France, there is a need to visit clients in the region as required (typically fortnightly basis).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world&lt;/strong&gt;: Your efforts will result in real-world impact—helping to keep the lights on, get food into grocery stores, and most importantly, ensure workers return home safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your mantra is &lt;strong&gt;#alwaysbeprospecting&lt;/strong&gt;: The world of operations is vast. Your customers are often out in the field and the best way to catch them is live on the phone. Samsara’s top reps do constant research to find companies and contacts to expand their pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have innate curiosity in how businesses work&lt;/strong&gt;: One day you’ll meet with someone in waste management and the next you may be learning about the inner workings of a food distribution center. Our top sales team members seek to learn the ins and outs of the businesses they support in order to make a larger impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are a life-long learner&lt;/strong&gt;: Samsara sales are complex. You will need to learn about businesses where you previously had little knowledge. The payoff is big but you have to be willing to put in the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You build genuine relationships with your customers&lt;/strong&gt;: The industries we serve have relied on pen-and-paper solutions for years and haven’t been met with the type of technology we offer. Our customers value earned trust and human relationships built over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best:&lt;/strong&gt; Samsara’s high-performance Sales culture means you’ll be surrounded by the best and challenged to go farther than you have before.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own your destiny:&lt;/strong&gt; Operate as a pure revenue leader, responsible for &lt;strong&gt;80-90% net-new logo acquisition&lt;/strong&gt; through self-sourced pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get In Early: &lt;/strong&gt;The France Mid-Market is a high-achieving segment in the company. The window to build something significant is open right now.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharpen Your Edge:&lt;/strong&gt; Access elite enablement — Command the Message and MEDDPICC coaching — built to make you a more effective closer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigate Complexity:&lt;/strong&gt; Move beyond feature-pushing to sell high-level ROI and safety outcomes to sophisticated economic buyers (MDs and FDs) in the field and the boardroom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Winning DNA:&lt;/strong&gt; A minimum of 18 months in a full-cycle, outbound-heavy SaaS closing role. You must have a proven history of building your own pipe from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verified Overachievement:&lt;/strong&gt; A track record of hitting and exceeding quota in a competitive, complex environment. We’ll want to see this on your resume.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Grit:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing multi-stakeholder deal cycles and technical POCs. We value your ability to hunt more than the brand name on your previous CV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native French&lt;/strong&gt; language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also offers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intellectual Curiosity:&lt;/strong&gt; You are eager to learn the inner workings of diverse industries, from waste management to food distribution, to better align our technology with their operational pain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Repeatable Sales Framework:&lt;/strong&gt; You don’t rely on luck or intuition. You have a structured methodology that delivers success and you understand that consistent, high-quality inputs lead to predictable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Data-Minded Approach:&lt;/strong&gt; You are a student of your own funnel. You understand how to structure your activity—prospecting volume, discovery depth, and multi-threading—to ensure a consistent output and forecast accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Process Iteration:&lt;/strong&gt; You possess a relentless drive for self-improvement. You are someone who actively seeks feedback, iterates on their approach, and understands that evolving your tactics is the only way to stay ahead of the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we build for the people who keep the global economy moving. We want owners, not passengers, which is why &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;our rewards&lt;/a&gt; are designed to fuel high-impact builders. Our compensation program delivers above-market total compensation through a combination of base salary, performance-based bonus/variable pay, and equity (for eligible roles) in a high-growth public company. We meaningfully differentiate pay for our top performers, who have the opportunity to earn above-market compensation that can outpace the broader market over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond compensation, we provide the foundations that enable long-term success: a flexible, employee-led remote model, a professional development stipend, comprehensive health and parental leave plans, and more. If you’re ready to build for the long term and own the outcome, your journey starts here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Samsara, we embrace a flexible working model that caters to the diverse needs of our teams. Our offices are open for those who prefer to work in-person and we also support remote work where it aligns with our operational requirements. For certain positions, being close to one of our offices or within a specific geographic area is important to facilitate collaboration, access to resources, or alignment with our service regions. In these cases, the job description will clearly indicate any working location requirements. Our goal is to ensure that all members of our team can contribute effectively, whether they are working on-site, in a hybrid model, or fully remotely. All offers of employment are contingent upon an individual’s ability to secure and maintain the legal right to work at the company and in the specified work location, if applicable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Belonging at Samsara&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we welcome everyone regardless of their background. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, disability, age, and other characteristics protected by law. We depend on the unique approaches of our team members to help us solve complex problems and want to ensure that Samsara is a place where people from all backgrounds can make an impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is an inclusive work environment, and we are committed to ensuring equal opportunity in employment for qualified persons with disabilities. Please email &lt;a ---------- or &lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/DrM6DFQUiSgfPtCVA&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; if you require any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Authenticity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use &lt;a href=&quot;https://hiretofu.com/privacyPolicy&quot;&gt;Tofu&lt;/a&gt;, a fraud detection tool, to validate the authenticity of applications and protect against identity fraud. This ensures we are connecting with real people and allows us to prioritize genuine candidates. Please see Samsara’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraudulent Employment Offers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is aware of scams involving fake job interviews and offers. Please know we do not charge fees to applicants at any stage of the hiring process. Official communication about your application will only come from emails ending in ----- ----- or ----- For more information regarding fraudulent employment offers, please visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://samsara.com/blog/avoiding-fake-job-offers&quot;&gt;blog post here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

Le Groupe Cybertek est un acteur majeur dans le secteur de la vente de matériel informatique et High-Tech en France. Créé en 1996, son siège social et ses plateformes logistiques se trouvent à Bordeaux. Cybertek possède 28 magasins sous les enseignes Cybertek et Grosbill, ainsi que cinq sites de commerce en ligne. Employant 270 personnes, Cybertek a réussi à atteindre un chiffre d'affaires annuel de plus de 100 millions d'euros en s’appuyant sur des équipes dynamiques et soudées. Le Groupe Cybertek affirme son engagement en faveur de l’égalité professionnelle entre les femmes et les hommes et veille à promouvoir un environnement de travail inclusif, notamment pour les personnes en situation de handicap.
Vos missions
Au cœur de nos magasins répartis sur toute la France lors de vos déplacements quotidiens, vous jouerez un rôle essentiel dans leur bon fonctionnement, l’accompagnement des équipes et le développement du chiffre d’affaires. 
Réaliser le suivi des magasins définis :

Vérifier et contribuer à la mise en place d’une organisation permettant d’assurer le bon fonctionnement du point de vente (application et respect des procédures internes) ;
Veiller et participer à l’amélioration de l’image de marque du point de vente (présentation, ponctualité, propreté, accueil des clients, accueil téléphonique, rappel des clients, relationnel, etc.) ;
Contrôler les points de vente (stocks, activités réalisées au sein du point de vente, horaires d’ouverture) ;
Contrôler et analyser l’activité commerciale du magasin (devis, commandes, factures, chiffre d’affaires, résultats, objectifs) ; 
Motiver, accompagner et soutenir les équipes ainsi que le Responsable dans le développement du chiffre d’affaires du point de vente ;
Assurer un soutien des équipes par une présence régulière dans chaque point de vente ;
Assurer les remplacements en magasin si nécessaires ;
Réaliser un entretien mensuel avec chaque Responsable afin d’évaluer l’avancement des objectifs, d’identifier les éventuelles difficultés et de prendre les décisions nécessaires en conséquence ;

Suivi des interventions et coordination avec la Direction :

Réaliser un rapport sur chaque passage et contrôle d’un point de vente 
Analyser les données ; 
Assurer un point régulier avec la Direction au cours d’entretiens ponctuels, par téléphone plusieurs fois par semaine ;
Organiser une réunion tous les quinze jours afin de réaliser un point détaillé sur chaque point de vente et de définir les futures interventions ;
Réaliser une réunion mensuelle avec la Direction afin de produire un bilan du mois écoulé et de définir les objectifs du mois suivant ;
Animer une réunion mensuelle avec les différents services du siège social du Groupe Cybertek en lien avec les magasins, afin d’identifier les difficultés rencontrées et d’améliorer la communication et la coordination entre les différents services (SAV, Technique, Stock, Administratif, etc.) ;

L’animation commerciale :

Animer les magasins et organiser les journées portes ouvertes (salons, partenariats, etc.) ;
Assurer le facing des magasins et veiller à la bonne présentation de l’offre produit et des produits en démonstration ;Assurer le suivi et le reporting des incentives et des différentes opérations commerciales.

Vos compétences
Vous justifiez d’une expérience dans le suivi et le contrôle de points de vente, idéalement dans le secteur de l’informatique ou de l’high-tech. Rigoureux(se), organisé(e) et doté(e) d’un bon relationnel, vous êtes à l’aise avec l’analyse des performances commerciales, le suivi des stocks et le contrôle du respect des procédures.
Vous savez accompagner et soutenir les équipes et les Responsables de magasin dans l’atteinte de leurs objectifs, tout en identifiant les éventuels axes d’amélioration. Autonome, réactif(ve) et force de proposition, vous appréciez le travail de terrain, les déplacements et les échanges avec les différents services.
Vous souhaitez évoluer dans un environnement dynamique et contribuer activement à la performance et au bon fonctionnement de nos points de vente ? Rejoignez notre équipe en tant que Contrôleur(se) Magasins !Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships – all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open – we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is WPP&#39;s AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;wppmedia.com&quot;&gt;wppmedia.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work-life-balance:&lt;/strong&gt; Teamwork and personal collaboration in the office are central to us, but we also offer a regular remote work day for added flexibility. In addition, you can compensate for overtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vacation mode on:&lt;/strong&gt; You receive 26 days of paid leave plus an additional 4 compensation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellbeing first:&lt;/strong&gt; Health benefits and dedicated Mental Health Awareness Days put your health and well-being front and center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practice makes perfect:&lt;/strong&gt; Grow through our diverse training programs and leverage internal career initiatives for your personal development across the WPP network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More than just a job:&lt;/strong&gt; Look forward to unforgettable team events, exclusive employee discounts, and many more highlights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be yourself:&lt;/strong&gt; Everyone is warmly welcome here – diversity and equal opportunities are at the core of who we are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is what you move:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Manager Media Solutions | Campaign (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;, you are responsible for the operational planning, coordination, and activation of digital campaigns for our&amp;nbsp;key global client Roche.&amp;nbsp;Your primary focus is on programmatic activations across CTV, Video, and DOOH. Based in the Media Solutions Unit Switzerland, you will work closely with Client Leads, Programmatic Specialists, local and international WPP teams, as well as publishers and technology partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign Activation:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently coordinate and activate programmatic campaigns with a clear focus on CTV, Video, and DOOH.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Campaign Roll-outs:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the execution of multinational campaigns across various markets, working closely with local WPP teams to identify the best publishers, ad inventories, and activation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setup, Monitoring &amp;amp; Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Campaign setup in relevant DSPs and activation platforms is in your hands, along with continuous delivery monitoring and data-driven performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner &amp;amp; Client Team Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a central interface with publishers, media vendors, and technology partners while advising client teams on feasibility checks and activation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Derive actionable insights from campaign reports and share best practices across involved teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processes &amp;amp; Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively document and enhance activation processes, drive competency growth in Programmatic, CTV, and DOOH, and contribute to evaluating new technologies as well as international projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The following qualities distinguish you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programmatic &amp;amp; Media Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid professional experience in digital media, programmatic advertising, campaign management, or ad operations – ideally within an agency, media owner, or adtech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform &amp;amp; AdTech Know-how:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with at least one leading DSP (e.g., DV360, The Trade Desk, Adform) along with a strong understanding of digital advertising ecosystems and adtech infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CTV &amp;amp; DOOH Specialization:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior exposure to Connected TV (CTV), Digital Video, and/or Digital Out-of-Home (DOOH), combined with an enthusiasm for cross-channel digital campaign formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organization &amp;amp; Project Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong organizational skills, a structured and solution-oriented work approach, and ease in managing complex campaign workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Team Spirit:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent communication skills, analytical thinking, and a collaborative mindset for cross-market teamwork in an international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Business-fluent English (written and spoken) for daily international collaboration; good German skills are a welcome plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Furthermore you are:&lt;strong&gt; #problem-solver #team-player #hands-on-mentality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this job sounds exciting to you, we strongly encourage you to apply, even if you don&#39;t have every qualification listed above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at WPP Media:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our passion for shaping the next era of media includes investing in our employees to help them do their best work, and we’re just as committed to employee growth as we are to responsible media investment. WPP Media employees can tap into the global WPP Media &amp;amp; WPP networks to pursue their passions, grow their networks, and learn at the cutting edge of marketing and advertising. We have a variety of employee resource groups and host frequent in-office events showcasing team wins, sharing thought leadership, and celebrating holidays and milestone events.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP Media is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to particular characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please read our privacy policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for Germany, Austria and Switzerland for further information on how we process the data you provide. #LI-Promoted 14018&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;Please read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy#:~:text=WPP%20Media%20Privacy%20Notice%20for%20Recruitment&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Climate Matters More Than Ever&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supply chain leaders are being asked to cut costs and carbon at the same time. Yet logistics and sustainability teams often work with different data, tools, and priorities. Meanwhile, regulations and industry standards are raising expectations for how companies measure and manage their emissions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most climate tools stop at reporting: a dashboard or a year-end PDF, produced long after a shipment has moved. They rarely reach the people deciding how to route goods, when to ship, or how much inventory to hold.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Climate team at Flexport is building emissions intelligence directly into the platform where supply chain decisions are made. We help customers weigh cost, speed, and emissions together—and turn that understanding into action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexport already runs the shipments, holds the data, and provides the platform where customers manage their supply chains. That puts us in a strong position to connect climate insights with the operational decisions that drive emissions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the primary engineer for Climate, working independently of our existing engineering teams and partnering closely with the Climate Manager, your main day-to-day business stakeholder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think of it as a small startup within Flexport: direct access to the business, a broad scope, and substantial ownership. Together with the Climate Manager, you will identify the most valuable problems to solve, shape the product direction, and turn ideas into reliable software. This role calls for someone who enjoys both deciding what to build and building it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things We ❤️&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning complex shipment and emissions data into clear, actionable choices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working directly with stakeholders and users to understand what would make their lives better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building simple, reliable products and learning from how people use them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finding opportunities where lower costs and lower emissions go together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking an idea from an ambiguous problem to a useful product in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Climate Programs Manager to understand customer needs, challenge assumptions, and translate business goals into a practical product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery from problem discovery and technical design through implementation, launch, operation, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build emissions intelligence into everyday supply chain decisions, including routing, transport mode, shipment timing, and inventory planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers identify opportunities to reduce emissions using Flexport’s shipment data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make lower-emission choices easier to understand and act on within existing workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop products that help customers understand the wider environmental footprint of their supply chains, beyond freight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver useful improvements incrementally, balancing speed, scope, maintainability, and data accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with other engineering teams when your work depends on shared systems, integrations, or expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure whether what you ship solves the underlying problem, and use that evidence to decide what comes next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Should Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience, with a strong engineering foundation and experience delivering production software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of working independently: you can bring structure to an unclear problem, set priorities, unblock yourself, and follow through without a detailed specification or constant direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment: you understand user needs, identify what is worth building, and make thoughtful tradeoffs between impact and effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with business stakeholders: you ask good questions, explain technical choices in plain language, and constructively challenge ideas when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to own features across the stack, including user interfaces, backend services, and data integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A love of simple, well-tested code that is easy to extend and hard to break.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort taking responsibility for the reliability and maintenance of what you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for action, combined with the judgment to recognize when you need input or help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An aptitude for learning quickly, including unfamiliar business domains and technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal motivation to work on climate and environmental challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in climate technology, emissions accounting, logistics, or supply chain software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products in a startup or another small team with broad ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning complex data into customer-facing insights and decision tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior climate experience is a plus; curiosity and the ability to learn the domain matter more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your day-to-day work will center on a close partnership with the Climate Manager, with collaboration across engineering as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will have substantial autonomy and will be expected to keep stakeholders aligned on priorities, progress, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We build and launch incrementally, using feedback to guide the next step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In Amsterdam, we come to the office two to three times a week to collaborate, whiteboard, and spend time together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexport’s broader technology stack includes React, TypeScript, Ruby on Rails, Kotlin, Kubernetes, GraphQL, gRPC, Postgres, Kafka, and Snowflake. We welcome candidates from different technology backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in It for You?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct ownership of products that help customers make better supply chain and environmental decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to shape Climate technology with the autonomy of a small startup and the reach of Flexport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity participation and a defined pension contribution scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 vacation days based on full-time employment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid premiums for Flexport’s collective health insurance plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunches, breakfast, snacks, and drinks in the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Covered home-to-office commuting costs for employees living outside Amsterdam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee assistance and parental leave benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;1704749847.557549&quot; class=&quot;c-virtual_list__item&quot; data-qa=&quot;virtual-list-item&quot; data-item-key=&quot;1704749847.557549&quot;&gt;
