With a legacy as a pioneer in the ALSP market, Factor has&nbsp;identified&nbsp;the need for another innovation in the legal services market: Integrated&nbsp;LawTM.&nbsp;


Factor is the market leader in Integrated&nbsp;LawTM, combining the&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;of Traditional Law, the efficiency of New Law, and the close business integration of In-house legal to deliver complex legal work at scale.&nbsp;


Factor works alongside corporate legal departments to solve for the ever-increasing demands and complexity of transactional legal work like contracting. We deliver better performance, better business and legal outcomes, and a better contracting experience.&nbsp;


 Our clients span Fortune 500 companies including global banks, major pharmaceutical&nbsp;companies&nbsp;and large technology firms.  &nbsp;


 Factor is committed to building the best culture in legal. We believe that the more diverse our team becomes — in backgrounds, skills, experiences, and perspectives — the higher our creative potential as a company. We are dedicated to growing a diverse, inclusive company where individuals of all backgrounds thrive.  &nbsp;


 We are comprised of more than 300 lawyers, legal specialists, technologists, and process consultants across Europe and North America-join us!


&nbsp;
THE ROLE:&nbsp;


We are seeking an experienced Company Secretary &amp; Legal Entity Management Senior Associate to oversee the governance, compliance, and administration of the company's global legal entity portfolio. This role is responsible for ensuring that all corporate entities operate in compliance with applicable statutory and regulatory requirements while maintaining strong corporate governance standards.
The successful candidate will partner closely with Legal, Finance, Tax, HR, and external advisers to manage entity lifecycle events, board governance activities, regulatory filings, and corporate records across multiple jurisdictions


&nbsp;
This is a permanent, full-time opportunity to join our Belfast Legal Entity Management team dedicated to providing support to our clients.Responsibilities: 
Corporate Governance &amp; Company Secretarial

Manage company secretarial activities for a global portfolio of legal entities.


Coordinate and support Board and Committee meetings, including agenda planning, preparation of board papers, minute taking, and follow-up actions.Ensure compliance with corporate governance frameworks, constitutional documents, and statutory obligations.


Maintain accurate statutory registers, corporate records, and governance documentation.


Provide governance advice and guidance to directors, senior leaders, and stakeholders.


&nbsp;
Legal entity related matters:&nbsp;


Oversee the maintenance and administration of domestic and international legal entities.


Manage the full entity lifecycle, including incorporations, dissolutions, liquidations, restructures, mergers, and acquisitions.Ensure timely completion of annual filings, regulatory submissions, licenses, and statutory requirements.


Maintain entity management databases and corporate record systems.


Coordinate with external corporate secretarial providers, law firms, and regulatory bodies.


&nbsp;
Compliance and Regulatory matters:&nbsp;


Monitor and assess changes in corporate governance and regulatory requirements across relevant jurisdictions.


Ensure adherence to local corporate laws, filing deadlines, and compliance obligations.


Support internal audits and compliance reviews relating to legal entities and governance matters.


Identify and mitigate governance and compliance risks.


Develop and enhance policies, procedures, and controls related to legal entity management


&nbsp;
This is a very exciting and unique opportunity to build a career locally but operate globally.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
If you believe in being a team player, can collaborate and communicate well with technical and non-technical audiences while bringing a result-driven, focused, high energy, confident, curious, quirky, and most of all fun sense of self, then this is the place for you
&nbsp; QUALIFICATIONS:
You are adaptable, authentic, accountable, and values-driven. You’re a team player who exhibits personal leadership and leaves things better than you found them. We’re looking for someone who always gives their best and inspires others to do the same.

&nbsp;
In addition to the above, here are the required skills, knowledge, capabilities, and education for this role:
&nbsp;
Essential Criteria&nbsp;

Undergraduate degree
4+ years company secretarial or Compliance/Regulatory experience
Experience leading/managing Board Meetings, Annual General Meetings and Extraordinary General Meetings
Excellent attention to detail
Regular client-facing experience
Good commercial awareness, working directly with business managers
Strong written and verbal communication and presentation skills
Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office, particularly Excel
Legally eligible to work in the United Kingdom&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Desirable Criteria&nbsp;

Familiarity with Blueprint Company Secretarial Software
Experience working within the financial services sector
Knowledge of companies legislation outside of the UK
Exposure to Pan-European investment structures
As a member of an ISO Compliant centre, the candidate will be required to follow the policies and procedures on Information Security Management System in place at the Centre of Excellence and globally at Factor. As a member of the Factor team, the applicant will have access to various company and client assets and will be required to maintain the level of security as identified for each asset.
&nbsp;
Factor is an Equal Opportunity Employer.
For more, visit:&nbsp;https://www.factor.law&nbsp;&nbsp;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

Established in 2004, OLIVER is the world's first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&nbsp;
As a part of The Brandtech Group, we're at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our AI solutions enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&nbsp;Role: Account Director (6 Month FTC)
Location: London/ Slough, United Kingdom&nbsp; (2-3 days a week from our Client's Slough Offices)
About the role:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
As Account Director, working within our client, &amp; global FMCG business; you are the trusted day-to-day partner for client and the person who keeps complex, multi-platform projects on track. You'll work closely with strategy, creative, production and account colleagues to turn briefs into effective campaigns, with a strong focus on social media and digital content. You'll be accountable for delivery, client satisfaction and project profitability across several projects at once.
What you will be doing:&nbsp;

Build a collaborative, trusted relationship with client stakeholders, acting as their first point of contact and protecting the brand across every project.
Stay close to the client to understand their needs, anticipate issues and resolve them early.
Be accountable for integrated creative projects from brief to fulfilment, maintaining client satisfaction throughout.
Work with strategy and account colleagues to shape social strategy and milestones for the client.
Agree campaign scope with the client, then produce estimates and timing plans in our internal scheduling system, including for complex, cross-platform social projects.
Schedule projects against the right internal resource and help source external resource where needed.
Partner with digital, video, photography and print producers to bring the right skills together for integrated campaigns.
Keep projects on process, on time and on budget, motivating and coordinating teams through tight deadlines.
Be responsible for the financial health of your projects, including profitability, forecasting accuracy and fee discussions. Make sure everyone understands the cost impact of delays, extra amends and re-briefs.
Report on project income accurately and on time, and escalate invoicing or estimate queries to senior account and business leadership.
Evaluate project results, both qualitative and quantitative, against the original objectives.
Guide internal stakeholders through production processes, and spot and act on ad hoc opportunities as they arise.

&nbsp;
What you need to be great in this role:&nbsp;

Experience managing digital and integrated campaigns in a creative or production agency, with a strong record of delivering across multiple platforms, particularly social media.
Ideally FMCG experience
Proficient to expert capability in Account Management and Project Management, with confidence running several complex projects at once.
Experience working alongside video and photography producers as part of a joined-up approach to campaign delivery.
Experience with project scheduling and sourcing resource and production services.
Strong client engagement skills, with the ability to organise, influence and build effective working relationships.
Clear, courteous communication across strategy, creative, production and client teams.
Close attention to detail, sound commercial awareness and a sharp eye for project risk.
Comfort integrating with a client-side team while maintaining a top-tier agency service.
Nice to have: experience creating content for CMS and e-commerce platforms.
Advanced use of Gen AI tools relevant to account management to improve output quality and efficiency
Experience designing AI-assisted workflows for yourself and your team
Agentic thinking for complex, multi-step challenges
Strong understanding of AI capabilities and limitations, with rigorous human oversight

