&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Detection and Response Engineer (Cheltenham, UK)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Cheltenham, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Product &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-Time, Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About VulnCheck&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exploitation prevention is only as strong as the intelligence driving those efforts, and most of the industry is still running on intelligence that lacks exploit context. VulnCheck, The exploit intelligence company, delivers structured exploit intelligence on what is actively weaponized in the wild, purpose-built for the data lakes, ETL pipelines, automation, and AI and LLM workflows your infrastructure already runs on, raising the capability of everything it powers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Target and Canary Intelligence products provide unique visibility into vulnerable assets on the internet, attacker infrastructure, and attacks that leverage vulnerabilities for initial access. Target Intelligence maintains a continuously updated view of internet-facing systems — the services and versions they run, and their exposure to vulnerabilities. Canary Intelligence deploys intentionally vulnerable systems across the internet and captures real exploitation attempts as they happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced detection and response engineer to help scale the durable detections behind these products. These detections generate world-class, vulnerability-centric threat intelligence our customers rely on to defend themselves against exploitation activity on the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have wide latitude to shape how VulnCheck stays ahead of an accelerating volume of vulnerabilities - the tooling, the workflows, and the standards for detection engineering at scale. Although this is a 100% remote role, candidates must be located in or around Cheltenham, United Kingdom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and direct AI-assisted, agentic detection workflows that scale coverage to an accelerating volume of vulnerabilities, with you on the loop for quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and ship network signatures and detections against internet-scale scan and probe data to identify services, versions, and whether hosts are vulnerable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build detections against Canary telemetry that separate real exploitation signal from internet noise, and synthesize that signal into threat intelligence customers can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive feedback loops into our probing and collection capabilities - identifying what data we should collect, what we shouldn&#39;t, and where coverage gaps exist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evaluate detection quality, measuring and tuning false positive and false negative rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond rapidly when high-impact vulnerabilities drop - analyze, build coverage, ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside our vulnerability researchers and threat hunters to connect detection engineering with exploit intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and shipping durable detections over network and host data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling detection development and continuous evaluation processes using AI and agentic workflows with humans on the loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of researching, engineering, and validating durable detections across network and host telemetry, with a disciplined approach to false positives and false negatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in device fingerprinting and protocol analysis. You understand the nuances of how services manifest on the wire, and how these signals stack to passively uncover what is running behind an open port on an internet address&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of attacker command-and-control techniques, covert channels, and exploitation artifacts — and how to identify them through network traffic analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in host-based analysis and DFIR. You know what telemetry is worth collecting from sensors to identify exploitation activity and attacker behaviors, and how to synthesize it into high-quality, actionable threat intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming or scripting ability — you can codify detection logic so it is performant and integrates cleanly with VulnCheck’s engineering system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CVE, NVD, KEV, or exploit intelligence datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A response mindset — when a new vulnerability drops, you&#39;re the first to dig in, analyze it, and ship detection coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and tuning detections in Suricata, Snort, Zeek, or similar, and writing Nuclei templates or other scanner signatures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published detection research, signatures, or open-source detection content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with streaming systems or real-time data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in high-growth or startup environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe people do their best work when they feel supported, trusted, and valued. VulnCheck offers benefits designed to meet a wide range of needs and lifestyles, tailored to your country of employment:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous, flexible time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement/pension plan contributions (e.g., 401k with match in the US; local pension schemes elsewhere)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive healthcare coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-friendly environment with flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for home office costs (phone &amp;amp; internet)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Specific benefit details vary by country and are confirmed during the offer process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built on over two decades of cybersecurity experience, our team of experts understands the intricacies of vulnerabilities, their exploitation in the wild, and how to leverage this data to build more effective cybersecurity products that produce better outcomes for organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VulnCheck gives organizations a tactical advantage by providing best-in-class exploit &amp;amp; vulnerability intelligence information. We have a sense of duty to protect the critical infrastructure we rely on including medical devices, power grids and telecommunication networks. We were founded in 2021 in Lexington, Massachusetts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VulnCheck has a transparent, collaborative, and supportive culture — we are looking for people who have a growth mindset, are curious and innovative. Our team is smart, but humble, hardworking, and supportive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VulnCheck is proud to be an Equal Employer Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. VulnCheck is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with physical and mental disabilities. &lt;em&gt;Even if your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly align with the job description, we encourage you to apply — we value potential just as much as a perfect resume.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Operations &amp;amp; Payroll (Working Student)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About the team&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, our People Operations &amp;amp; Payroll team is the engine behind a smooth and reliable employee experience. We manage the full employee lifecycle — from onboarding and contract changes through to offboarding — while supporting accurate and timely payroll across Southern Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In France, recurring operational work is growing across employee lifecycle administration, field sales hiring and payroll coordination. You’ll join a hands-on, detail-driven team where operational excellence and employee care go hand in hand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;The role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Working Student position supporting the People Operations &amp;amp; Payroll team in France. You’ll take ownership of recurring administrative and payroll support tasks, help keep our data accurate and up to date, and make sure employees and managers get timely, clear support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a great entry point into HR and payroll operations for someone who is organised, reliable, and eager to build real expertise in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payroll support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to collect, and organise payroll input data ahead of monthly deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support follow-up with external payroll and benefits providers where relevant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain accurate payroll records and flag missing information or discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HR administration &amp;amp; employee lifecycle&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, update, and archive employment contracts and employee documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding, contract changes, and offboarding processes — ensuring data accuracy and completeness at every step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with benefits administration where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employee support &amp;amp; ticket handling&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to routine employee and manager queries via internal systems and email with clarity and care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage open tickets and follow up, escalating more complex cases when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data management &amp;amp; process improvement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and update employee data in HR systems and Excel / Google Sheets trackers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform regular data checks and keep Notion pages and internal documentation up to date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify repetitive steps, data-quality issues, or bottlenecks in recurring workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suggest small process improvements that make day-to-day operations more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently studying or recently graduated in HR, Business Administration, Economics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in French and English — clear written and verbal communication is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a commitment to accuracy, especially with sensitive employee and payroll data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Excel / Google Sheets skills and confidence working with structured data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organised and reliable — able to manage recurring tasks and meet regular deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable handling confidential information with discretion and good judgement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick to learn new tools and systems — we work across multiple HR platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player with a hands-on, service-oriented attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Previous experience or studies in HR, payroll administration, or people operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Interest in payroll processes, HR systems, or process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Familiarity with AI tools such as ChatGPT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Why SumUp?&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎&amp;nbsp; Work with a truly global, multicultural team from our Barcelona office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈&amp;nbsp; Be part of a workplace that values diversity and inclusion, where every perspective is respected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;❤️&amp;nbsp; Access our Employee Assistance Programme for mental health guidance and support when you need it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_8220454926977230902gmail-docs-internal-guid-9a9f34f4-7fff-014a-c97c-98ca90610a47&quot;&gt;Algolia is the retrieval intelligence layer that turns intent into trusted, decision-grade outcomes. Powering more than 1.7 trillion queries a year for over 18,000 customers with millisecond latency and 99.999% reliability, we are the recognized leader for Search and Product Discovery by top industry analyst firms. The Algolia platform turns a company&#39;s products, content, and business rules into data that humans, applications and AI agents can act upon. The result is trusted customer experiences with stronger conversions for measurable business impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Site Reliability Engineer to join the Search team. We are responsible for the cloud-based scalable architecture for NeuralSearch, our AI search engine, which incorporates both keyword and vector search. Our work consists of distributed components which orchestrate the building and storage of indices containing customer data and then querying that data to return search results. The role requires understanding and solving the challenges that come with complex distributed systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is composed of engineers, most of whom are fully remote, with different skill sets and backgrounds. Your experience, your knowledge and your perspective will add to this diversity and help the team deliver products that make a difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU WILL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a key contributor to the design and development of the Search and Indexing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for operations for the Search system including participation in out-of-hours on-call rota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a full-remote team, with the option to be either full-remote, hybrid or office based (Paris) yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for the quality and soundness of the system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share your expertise on distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with other teams to identify, troubleshoot and resolve high impact issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU MIGHT BE A FIT IF YOU HAVE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating distributed systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large datasets and high traffic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigor in high code quality, automated testing, and other engineering best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent spoken and written English skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at our current stage and beyond ($50-200M ARR range, high growth, lots of change and building internal infrastructure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Algolia does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, military status, veteran status, disability status, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary compensation range for this role reflects market pay data within this location. The exact compensation offered for this role may vary depending on specific location and job-related knowledge, technical skills, and experience; and is only one part of our Total Rewards philosophy to compensate and recognize employees for their work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€70.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€97.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLEXIBLE WORKPLACE STRATEGY:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Algolia’s flexible workplace model is designed to empower all Algolians to fulfill our mission to power search and discovery with ease. We place an emphasis on an individual’s impact, contribution, and output, over their physical location. Algolia is a high-trust environment and many of our team members have the autonomy to choose where they want to work and when.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a global presence with offices in Paris, NYC, London, Sydney and Bucharest, however we also offer many of our team members the option to work remotely either as fully remote or hybrid-remote employees.&lt;strong&gt; Positions listed as &quot;Remote&quot; are only available for remote work within the specified country. Positions listed within a specific city are only available in that location - depending on the role it may be available with either a hybrid-remote or in-office schedule.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE’RE LOOKING FOR SOMEONE WHO CAN LIVE OUR VALUES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRIT&lt;/strong&gt; - Problem-solving and perseverance capability in an ever-changing and growing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TRUST &lt;/strong&gt;- Willingness to trust our co-workers and to take ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CANDOR&lt;/strong&gt; - Ability to receive and give constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CARE&lt;/strong&gt; - Genuine care about other team members, our clients and the decisions we make in the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HUMILITY&lt;/strong&gt; - Aptitude for learning from others, putting ego aside.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for talented, passionate people to help build the world’s best search and discovery technology. We value autonomy, diversity, and collaboration. We’re committed to creating an inclusive workplace where everyone is respected and supported—regardless of race, age, ancestry, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, marital status, color, veteran status, disability, or socioeconomic background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT NOTICE FOR CANDIDATES - Recruitment Fraud Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve recently seen an increase in recruitment scams targeting job seekers. To help protect yourself, please keep the following in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our open positions may appear on third-party job boards, but the &lt;strong&gt;best way to apply safely&lt;/strong&gt; is directly through our &lt;strong&gt;careers page&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All genuine communication from Algolia will come from an ----- email address. If you receive an email from someone claiming to work at Algolia who does not have an ----- email address, please do not respond or share any personal information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’ll &lt;strong&gt;never ask for payments, purchases, or financial details&lt;/strong&gt; during the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;READY TO APPLY?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you share our values and our enthusiasm for building the world’s best search &amp;amp; discovery technology, we’d love to review your application!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;Avec une stratégie de croissance, le groupe Capco renforce le développement de son pôle FRC (Finance, Risques &amp;amp; Conformité) et tout particulièrement son offre Risque, et recherche pour son bureau parisien des Senior consultant(e)s pour accompagner ses clients sur leurs enjeux de transformation réglementaire et organisationnelle liés au risque de crédit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Votre rôle&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous participez, pour nos clients du secteur financier, à des missions variées qui couvrent plusieurs thématiques :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accompagnement dans la gestion de projets de mise en conformité réglementaire&amp;nbsp;: analyse des textes réglementaires, gap analysis méthodologique/système/data/gouvernance/processus, préconisations et mise en œuvre, documentation et accompagnement du changement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation à des missions d’inspections et des exercices de supervision (QIS, Benchmarking, Stress Testing, TRIM, mission d’homologation) : cadrage, coordination, documentation, traitement des recommandations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mise en place et optimisation de dispositif d’encadrement et de suivi des risques de crédit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refonte des processus d’octroi ou revue de dossier, de surveillance et de reporting des risques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Au sein de Capco&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participer à l’animation de la communauté Risques (veille réglementaire, supports de communication, Points of view, évènements clients, etc.),&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Le profil recherché&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne expertise de l’environnement des banques ainsi que des sujets de transformation de la fonction Finance et Risque au sein d’institutions financières ou bancaires.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connaissance de la règlementation : IRRBB, NDOD, ALM, IFRS9, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Target Operating Model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mise en place de reporting règlementaire (Corep, Finrep et Pilier 3)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revue de modèle en Liquidité et Solvabilité&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un excellent relationnel et un bon esprit d’équipe, vous avez envie d’accompagner activement la croissance d’un cabinet dynamique qui mise sur le management de proximité et vous êtes reconnu pour votre flexibilité et votre créativité. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne appétence et mobilité pour travailler avec un réseau de consultants à dimension internationale au service de nos clients en France et à l’étranger. La maîtrise du français et de l’anglais en langues de travail est indispensable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience de 5 ans minimum dans un cabinet de conseil, ou en gestion de projet au sein d’une institution financière. Vous êtes doté d’un diplôme Bac+5 de type école de commerce ou d’ingénieur ou universitaire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Qui sommes-nous&amp;nbsp;?&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Créé en 1998, Capco est un cabinet de conseil en management et en organisation spécialisé dans le secteur des services financiers. Avec 35 bureaux répartis en Europe, en Asie et en Amérique, Capco regroupe 7 000 collaborateurs dont 180 en France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depuis plus de 20 ans, Capco Paris accompagne les établissements financiers français et internationaux grâce à une réflexion innovante et une expertise dans les domaines bancaires.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi choisir Capco&amp;nbsp;?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Créé en 1998, Capco est un cabinet de conseil en management et en organisation spécialisé dans le secteur des services financiers, avec 35 bureaux répartis entre l’Amérique, l’Asie et l’Europe et regroupant 7 000 collaborateurs dont 180 à Paris.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre offre conseil s’appuie sur trois grands domaines d’expertise&amp;nbsp;: Business Consulting, Digital et Techonology&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Capco, nous vous offrons&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
