&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help make the world more hospitable &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hospitality industry is uniquely human, and it deserves technology that’s just as inspiring as the people behind it. At Mews, we’re transforming the industry with a platform that helps hotels run smarter, move faster and create better guest experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do. You’ll have autonomy and the trust to make good decisions and move quickly. And you’ll enjoy a real sense of purpose as you see the impact of what we’re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated by ownership, curiosity and meaningful impact, and are driven to deliver consistent high performance, you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&#39;s get into the specifics. It’s impossible to capture every nuance of a role – especially at a rapidly growing company like Mews – but if we had to distil it into a job description (which we do because this is a job description), it would be this:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be the founding analytics engineer in Finance, shaping our data infrastructure and analytical capabilities during a critical transformation. Your expertise in Python, &lt;span data-highlighted=&quot;true&quot; data-vc=&quot;highlighted-text&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_kqswh2mm&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_5pioz8co _189e1dm9 _1il9buyh _19lc184f _d0altlke&quot; data-testid=&quot;definition-highlighter&quot;&gt;DBT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, SQL, and Databricks will drive operational efficiency, accelerate our month-end close, and deliver strategic insights that inform capital allocation and IPO readiness. This is a greenfield opportunity to own the analytics roadmap, work directly with Finance leadership, and build infrastructure that powers both scaling and compliance, all at a pivotal moment for Mews&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you would do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop analytical features that surface actionable insights for Finance leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, optimise and maintain production-ready ETL/ELT pipelines using DBT, Databricks and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable data models and analytical solutions using modern data modelling techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and champion data quality and testing practices; catch errors before they reach stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Finance to translate business requirements into technical implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for modern data practices and continuous improvement of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you would bring&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on production experience building and optimising ETL/ELT pipelines (minimum 3 years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and Python; strong experience with DBT or equivalent modern data transformation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Databricks or similar cloud data platforms, or willingness to ramp quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data modelling and analytics architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working autonomously and managing priorities with ambiguity; ability to break down complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated commitment to data quality, testing and accuracy; take pride in work that&#39;s been thoroughly validated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency Level 3:&lt;/strong&gt; In this role, you&#39;ll redesign how Finance approaches data discovery and analysis using AI—not just automating your own work, but building patterns and tools that shape how the whole team questions data and validates insights. You&#39;ll use AI to accelerate model development and testing, but critically, you&#39;ll actively question what it produces and know when to push back. You&#39;ve built processes others follow; here, you&#39;ll do that with AI as a core enabler.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on AI fluency at Mews, please refer to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current&quot; href=&quot;https://mews.atlassian.net/wiki/x/XQOskg&quot;&gt;AI Fluency at Mews: A Comprehensive Guide for Candidates&lt;/a&gt; on Confluence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data visualisation tools like Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with regulated or governed data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling analytics in fast-growing startups or scale-ups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Spain&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€46.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€65.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Czechia&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;867 000 Kč&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;1 598 000 Kč CZK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;UK&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£49,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£55,500 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;France&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€54.500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€65.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency at Mews&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary ranges are provided in good faith and reflect current market conditions and internal pay structures. Final compensation may be adjusted based on funding, budget constraints, or exceptional candidate qualifications, but will remain within reasonable proximity to the stated range.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary disclosure is provided in compliance with applicable pay transparency legislation. We are committed to equal pay practices and prohibit salary history inquiries during our recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If the location you&#39;re applying from wasn&#39;t originally advertised for this role, salary range information is available upon request at any point during the application/interview process - your recruiter will be able to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our success is powered by our incredible people, supported by benefits that help them thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No matter where you’re based, you’ll enjoy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid holiday (yes, really)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in our company share program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave (6 months fully paid for primary caregivers, 2 months for secondary, available after one year of service)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual Learning budget of €300 (and more for high performers) to support your development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly &quot;EDGE&quot; time to Explore, Develop, Grow, and Elevate yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work from anywhere policy with flexibility to work abroad for a few weeks each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation options, available after one year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, hybrid working options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A home office setup budget to make your workspace your own and a monthly work-from-home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Claude tokens, so you can automate workflows and build smarter, more efficient ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll receive additional benefits that vary by location, from healthcare and retirement plans to team events, socials and other perks. Ask us about it during your interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Mews&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunities employer. We value teams that reflect the diversity of the customers and communities we serve. Different perspectives make better ideas, stronger products and a more welcoming company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also believe transparency is important when deciding if you&#39;re the right fit. Mews is an ambitious, high-pressure environment of continuous learning and high standards. Success here requires resilience, adaptability and a willingness to solve difficult problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few things that define how we work:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy means high responsibility. People are expected to take ownership and drive outcomes. There isn’t a detailed playbook for everything, and that’s part of what makes the work challenging – and rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change is constant. We’re growing quickly and adapting as we scale. Teams, processes and priorities continue to evolve, and only people who stay curious and agile will thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re remote-first, not relationship-free. Flexibility is core to how we work, but strong relationships still matter. Our teams are global, so we need expert collaborators and communicators to help us move forward together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI is an integral part of our processes. It’s not here to steal people’s jobs, but to amplify efficiency and productivity. We’re motivated to proactively use the technology to seek out better ways of working and share our findings with the rest of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there&#39;s anything we can do to support you during the application process, let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability or any other protected characteristic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One final thing: don&#39;t hold back. If you don&#39;t meet 100% of the criteria in this job description but you&#39;re certain you could make a big impact, apply. Everyone should have equal access to opportunities, and we&#39;re committed to providing an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If Mews sounds like the kind of environment where you&#39;d thrive, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

Une révolution en marche
&nbsp;
Nous sommes à l'aube d'une transformation majeure qui redéfinit le paysage tech. Chez Thiga, nous sommes convaincus que l'Intelligence Artificielle n'est pas juste une tendance - c'est une révolution qui transforme fondamentalement la façon dont nous concevons et développons des produits. Notre ambition? Être les pionniers de cette révolution agentique qui renforce les connexions humaines.
&nbsp;
Notre vision
&nbsp;
Nous croyons que l'IA va redéfinir :
- La façon dont nous concevons et développons des produits
- La manière dont les équipes créent des produits
- La manière dont les consultants font du conseil
&nbsp;
Une opportunité unique
&nbsp;
Nous sommes à un moment charnière où tout est possible. Chez Thiga, nous sommes Market Maker, c’est dans notre ADN depuis 10 ans. Nous montons une équipe R&amp;D qui va nous permettre de réinventer le Product Management dans l'industrie tech.
&nbsp;
En tant que Product Builder et/ou Product Manager IA, tu seras en immersion au sein des équipes de nos clients. Tu travailleras pour des sociétés allant de la Startup française au grand groupe international, dans des secteurs variés, pour identifier et développer des opportunités IA qui créent de la valeur.
&nbsp;
Ta mission :
&nbsp;
Exploration et Innovation
&nbsp;
- Identifier des opportunités IA pour nos clients et pour le cabinet
- Prototyper rapidement des solutions agentiques avec des outils no code/low code (V0, n8n, etc.)
- Réaliser une veille permanente et explorer les dernières innovations&nbsp;
- Évaluer et sélectionner les technologies IA pertinentes
- Participer à notre équipe R&amp;D pour positionner Thiga comme leader du marché
&nbsp;
Expertise produit &amp; IA
&nbsp;
- Établir une vision produit "claire" et identifier les incertitudes liées à l'IA
- Définir la stratégie et roadmap de produits IA
- Implémenter et intégrer des capacités d'IA dans les applications
- Faire vivre le cycle de vie de produits IA, de l‘expérimentation à la généralisation
- Définir les MVP et itérations qui permettront d'atteindre la vision
- Analyser les performances des solutions IA et identifier les leviers d'amélioration
&nbsp;
Accompagnement au changement
&nbsp;
- Comprendre les impacts organisationnels des solutions IA proposées
- Concevoir et déployer des stratégies d'adoption adaptées aux différentes parties prenantes
- Identifier et lever les résistances potentielles face à l'IA
- Accompagner la montée en compétence des équipes et utilisateurs sur les nouvelles solutions
- Mesurer l'adoption et ajuster les approches pour maximiser l'impact
&nbsp;
Tu as le profil si :
&nbsp;
- Tu as une très bonne culture IA : tu connais les champs d'application et les enjeux de la création de produits basés sur l'IA générative
- Tu comprends ce qu'est un système agentique et ses applications potentielles
- Tu comprends les concepts clés de prompt engineering et RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) avec expérience pratique des LLMs (directement et via API)
- Tu es capable de prototyper rapidement des solutions IA via des outils no code/low code
- Tu maîtrises les pratiques agiles (méthodo Scrum &amp; Kanban)
- Les méthodes de création de produits numériques comme le Design Thinking et le Lean Startup n'ont plus de secret pour toi
- Tu sais adopter le bon niveau de discours pour aligner des équipes techniques et métier
- You speak English
&nbsp;
Les petits plus :
&nbsp;
- Tu maîtrises les frameworks IA comme LangChain, LlamaIndex ou similaires
- Tu as de l'expérience concrète avec les systèmes agentiques
- Tu as de l'expérience avec les applications IA multimodales (voix, vision, texte)
- Tu as une compréhension des architectures cloud pour déployer des solutions IA
&nbsp;
Pourquoi nous rejoindre ? tu aimes :
&nbsp;
- Travailler sur différents projets clients chaque année, explorant constamment de nouvelles idées
- Faire partie d'une équipe&nbsp; passionnée et collaborative qui redéfinit le développement produit avec l'IA
- Les projets clients stimulants et variésUne culture d'entreprise qui valorise la curiosité et l'innovation
- Contribuer à une adoption réussie et éthique de l'IA dans les organisations
&nbsp;
Notre culture
&nbsp;
Chez Thiga, nous vivons selon des principes forts :
&nbsp;
Product first
&nbsp;
Nous pensons produit dans sa globalité, de l'expérience utilisateur jusqu'à l'infrastructure.
&nbsp;
Hands-on or nothing
&nbsp;
Notre approche est radicalement pratique. Nous croyons en la démonstration concrète plutôt qu'en la théorie.
&nbsp;
Market Maker by Design
&nbsp;
Nous repoussons les limites et partageons ouvertement nos innovations.
&nbsp;
Knowledge Open Bar
&nbsp;
Le savoir n'a de valeur que lorsqu'il est largement partagé. Nous diffusons librement nos apprentissages et nos outils.
&nbsp;
Thiga accueille toutes les personnes compétentes et passionnées et s'engage en faveur de la diversité culturelle, l'égalité de genre et l'emploi des travailleurs handicapés — au contraire nous considérons la diversité comme une grande richesse 
&nbsp;
#ProductManager #IA #Innovation #AIAgents #ProductInnovation #MarketMaker #GenerativeAI #LLM #AIRevolutionFind more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who is Tenable?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenable® is the Exposure Management company. Over 40,000 organizations around the globe rely on Tenable to understand and reduce cyber risk. Our global employees support 65 percent of the Fortune 500, 50 percent of the Global 2000, and large government agencies. Come be part of our journey!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes Tenable such a great place to work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ask a member of our team and they’ll answer, “Our people!” We work together to build and innovate best-in-class cybersecurity solutions for our customers; all while creating a culture of belonging, respect, and excellence where we can be our best selves. When you’re part of our #OneTenable team, you can expect to partner with some of the most talented and passionate people in the industry, and have the support and resources you need to do work that truly matters. We deliver results that exceed expectations and we win together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Your Role:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Regional Sales Director is responsible for leading France &amp;amp; BeneLux sales teams of highly skilled, seasoned sales individuals. The Regional Sales Director will map the course, develop the vision, implement annual plans and is accountable for delivering measurable results that achieves and exceeds revenue and margin targets for 2026 and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Your Opportunity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Act as the front-line manager for the French and BeneLux team.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Accurately manage, inspect and report in a predictable manner on all aspects of pipeline development and forecasts for the region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work closely with new as well as established channel partners to generate new business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop go to market plan for your specific region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead negotiations for large complex deals.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work closely with leadership for other functions such as Sales Engineering, Channel, finance, legal, R&amp;amp;D and marketing to ensure efficient alignment to regional activities and to enable optimum sales performance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Direct sales responsibility for accounts in the region and attain revenue goal for new product sales.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Initiate, establish and maintain contact with team members, prospects, clients, and partners within assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop recommendations for growth, opportunities for growth, and key target accounts in the assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a complete knowledge of Tenable’s products.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage active field presence by traveling up to 50% of the time across the France and BeneLux regions to meet with clients, partners, and team members.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;​&lt;b&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;10+ years of senior level management experience of direct reports in a fast paced, highly competitive, ever-changing sales environment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Min 6 years experience selling Security Products: Vulnerability Management, Continuous Monitoring, IDS/IPS, SIEM, DLP, Compliance, Encryption, access Management, Authentication, etc.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge and understanding on how to sell multi-product software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of MEDDPICC.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Focus on forecast quality and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 8+ years in quota carrying sales role with demonstrated success.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience negotiating large complex deals with extremely complex terms, conditions, price pressures and considerations.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Proven track record working with channel and technology partners to build strategic and cooperative sales campaigns together.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Strong command of English and French.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;History of coordination within an internal set of multi-functional teams such as Sales Engineers, Inside Reps, Field Marketing, Professional Services, and Channel Management to ensure target quotas as achieved and exceeded.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Reference-able domain expertise of the French and BeneLux region, accounts, decision makers and channel partner.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Be a coach to your direct team, as well as a keen interest in raising the bar in the entire team covering the region.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to accommodate up to 50% travel for regional business needs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;#LI-AV1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the expected salary range for this position in the primary job location, depending on experience and qualifications.&amp;nbsp;Compensation for the role will depend on a number of factors, including the candidate&#39;s qualifications, skills, competencies, location and experience, and may fall outside of the range shown. Employees are also eligible for variable compensation in addition to base pay (commission for sales roles, bonus for non-sales roles), depending on company and individual performance. Tenable also offers a variety of Competitive wellness and financial benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;EU Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€117.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€156.333,33 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We’re committed to promoting Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) at Tenable - through all equal employment opportunity laws and regulations at the international, federal, state and local levels.&amp;nbsp; If you need a reasonable accommodation due to a disability during the application or recruiting process, please contact&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;&lt;a ----- ----- for further assistance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tenable Data Consent Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenable is committed to protecting the privacy and security of your personal data. Depending on your location, one or more of the following notices may apply to you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static.tenable.com/marketing/hr/Tenable_General_Applicant_Privacy_Notice_FINAL_4-29-2026_branded.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;General Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static.tenable.com/marketing/hr/Tenable_CCPA_Notice_Applicants_FINAL_4-29-2026_branded.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static.tenable.com/marketing/hr/Tenable_EEA_UK_Applicant_Privacy_Notice_FINAL_6-4-2026_branded.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EU/EEA/UK Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are the platform turning browsing into shopping&lt;/strong&gt;. We connect 200 million shoppers with deals they love while boosting local sales for hundreds of top retailers and brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help consumers save time and money while making smart shopping decisions, and we support retailers and brands in engaging customers from online research to in-store purchases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2024, Shopfully joined forces with the North American company &lt;a href=&quot;https://corp.flipp.com/&quot;&gt;Flipp&lt;/a&gt;, creating a global leader in the sector. Together, we reach 400 million households and serve over 1,000 top retailers and brands across 27 markets, including Europe, Canada, the USA, Latin America, and Australia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;spark&lt;/strong&gt; your growth with us?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE LOOK FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 🦄&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flipp + Shopfully’s Product team focuses on driving adoption and revenue of our products by identifying the biggest market opportunities, building the case for investing in them, and shipping solutions with engineering, all while representing the voice of our merchant customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Product Manager is a senior, commercially minded product leader who already understands digital advertising. This role requires a strong strategic thinker with good business sense and solid hands-on product skills who leads opportunity identification, builds decision-ready business cases, and works with engineering to ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Sales, Engineering, Data, and Marketing teams across markets to align on key business objectives. By combining market insight, customer feedback, and industry trends, you will make sure our products resonate with merchants and drive growth. We’re looking for someone who can ramp up quickly and contribute independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL DO &lt;/strong&gt;🏄&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Understanding and Opportunity Identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Marketing, Sales Engineering and customer-facing teams to understand customer needs and prioritize the opportunities that matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find the highest-leverage areas to invest in, and weigh customer demand against our resources, capabilities and strategic direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex questions into clear priorities. For example: how do we create more value for retail partners as their strategies move toward e-commerce? How do we find and build opportunities at scale as products launch in new markets?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Cases and Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases that size opportunities, weigh revenue trade-offs, and structure a clear recommendation so leadership can make a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your recommendations, and be ready to explain them and adapt them as you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy for how our products differentiate from competitors in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Finance on pricing and monetization so our offering stays cohesive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Discovery and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with merchants, advertisers, and internal teams to define problems worth solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritise ruthlessly, balancing revenue impact, effort, and strategic fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with engineering to define requirements and ship, from alpha and testing through broad launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Marketing on launch timing and readiness, and run retrospectives on past launches to improve future ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignment and Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate cross-functional alignment (Engineering, Data, Sales, Marketing, Content) with a shared focus on goals and timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across markets and levels of seniority, including senior leadership, with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track progress and impact of product initiatives and communicate results clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with industry analysts, partners, and customers, and represent Flipp + Shopfully at conferences and industry events where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL NEED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;🪄&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital advertising foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; supply vs. demand, how exchanges, SSPs, and DSPs work, programmatic bidding, pricing models (CPM, CPC, CPV), and fill rate and yield. Ideally gained in ad tech, a retail media network, a publisher, or a marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building business cases: sizing opportunities, weighing revenue trade-offs, and structuring recommendations for decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High autonomy: you figure things out, own the outcome and don’t need close management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine excitement about using AI tools and rethinking how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on product skills: discovery, prioritisation, and working with engineering to ship, not only strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management, with the confidence to work across markets and levels of seniority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A scrappy, curious and confident approach. You’re hungry to make an impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 At our company, we value diversity and actively encourage it — we believe a variety of perspectives and backgrounds makes us stronger. We focus on potential rather than on having a “perfect” CV. If this role excites you and you believe you could grow into it — even if you don’t tick every single box in the requirements — we’d love to hear from you!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎆&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retail, CPG, or retail media background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-market experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can speak Italian or German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION 🌐&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have offices in Milan, Berlin, Barcelona, you can benefit from our flexible hybrid model (full remote available), empowering you to work where you&#39;re most effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOURS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;⏰&lt;br&gt;Your manager and several partner teams are in North America, so you’ll need to be flexible about working some later hours, beyond a standard 9-5 CET.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU WILL FIND AT SHOPFULLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; 🤗&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 An opportunity to thrive in a rapidly scaling multinational company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🕶️ A vibrant, informal, and inclusive work environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 We champion autonomy, flexibility, and a hybrid work model, empowering you to own your work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 Access to learning opportunities and regular feedback sessions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍓 Enjoy our central, modern offices featuring fresh snacks, coffee (including vegan options!), and ergonomic setups&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 Engage in meaningful team events: offsites, happy hours, company parties and celebrations that unite us beyond daily tasks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻We provide all the necessary equipment for you to work effectively and set up your workspace, wherever you are&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧰 Benefit from additional country-specific advantages based on local contracts and practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE &lt;/strong&gt;💜&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of 450 people (and counting!), from 30 different nationalities. We’re on a mission to innovate, and we believe the key to that is seeing the world through a variety of perspectives. That’s why building a more diverse team, as well as bringing in even more talent, is so important for us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TO FEEL AT HOME 🛋️ IN SHOPFULLY YOU NEED 🎯&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progress Over Perfection&lt;/strong&gt;: We move forward. Always. In a fast-moving world, speed with purpose beats certainty without action. Momentum matters—not for its own sake, but because it drives results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity Through Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;: We bring each other along. We work in teams, not silos. Transparency gives context, and context enables action. That means we share decisions early, publish work in progress, and document outcomes so others can learn, move faster, and build better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn Loudly&lt;/strong&gt;: We grow by doing and by daring. Big bets unlock big breakthroughs. But real innovation demands risk, and risk always carries the possibility of failure. That’s not a flaw. It’s the price of ambition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Challenge with Empathy&lt;/strong&gt;: We speak up, even when it’s hard—because candor shows care, and leads to better outcomes. Listening deeply is how we grow. Disagreeing openly is how we build trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always Build Better: We are builders—of products, systems, and ideas. But more than that, we are builders of better. Better has no finish line. It’s a mindset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you choose to apply for this specific job position and submit your application, which may include personal data such as your identifying details, contact information, curriculum vitae, cover letter, professional qualifications, and/or employment history, please be informed that your data may be shared with our Affiliates*, including Offerista Group GmbH and Flipp Operations Inc. The aforementioned entities will act as joint controllers for the limited purpose of intra-group sharing related to the evaluation of candidates’ applications. This means that your data may be processed by the Affiliate to assess your application and, if deemed suitable, to contact you regarding potential employment opportunities. However, please note that from the moment an Affiliate initiates direct contact with you and engages in any further processing of your personal data beyond the initial intra-group sharing for evaluation purposes, such Affiliate shall act as an independent data controller. In such cases, the processing of your personal data will be subject to the specific privacy policies that can be found&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://shopfully.com/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;* Affiliates shall mean any entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by or is under common control with ShopFully SpA and its Affiliates’ subsidiaries, meaning any entity which is directly or indirectly controlled by the Affiliates.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Support You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Total Rewards philosophy is to ensure that you are rewarded for impact, take part in accelerated career growth, thrive with highly flexible benefits, and are empowered to do your best work in a remote-first environment. In alignment with our overall Total Rewards Philosophy, we believe compensation should be fair, clear, consistent, and aligned to growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Italy Base Hiring Range:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€50.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€70.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in France on Arbeitnow

At&nbsp;CesiumAstro, we are developers and pioneers of out-of-the-box communication systems for satellites, UAVs, launch vehicles, and other space and airborne platforms. We take pride in our dynamic and cross-functional work environment, which allows us to learn, develop, and engage across our organization. If you are looking for hands-on, interactive, and autonomous work, CesiumAstro is the place for you. We are actively seeking passionate, collaborative, energetic, and forward-thinking individuals to join our team.
We are looking to add a Senior Sales Support Technician to our team. In this position, you will&nbsp;support the preparation, setup, and execution of aerospace communications demonstrations, field tests, and customer engagement activities. Working closely with the Sales Consultant and engineering teams, this role assists in deploying and operating satellite communication systems, RF hardware, ground station equipment, and related technologies used to demonstrate product capabilities to prospective customers and partners.&nbsp;
This position plays an important role in supporting technical demonstrations, validating system performance in real-world environments, and ensuring equipment and systems are properly configured for successful customer engagements. The Communications Technician will also support equipment maintenance, test preparation, and troubleshooting activities while helping translate technical system capabilities into successful customer demonstration experiences.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

Support the preparation, setup, and operation of aerospace communication systems used in customer demonstrations and technical presentations.&nbsp;
Assist with deployment and configuration of ground station equipment, antennas, RF systems, satellite communication terminals, and related hardware.&nbsp;
Participate in field demonstrations, trade shows, and customer engagement events to help showcase system capabilities.&nbsp;
Work closely with Sales Consultants and technical teams to ensure demonstrations accurately represent system performance and capabilities.
Prepare and configure communications equipment, hardware, and software prior to customer demonstrations or test activities.&nbsp;
Assist in validating system performance and verifying that equipment is operating correctly prior to demonstrations.&nbsp;
Support integration and connectivity between ground systems, communication payloads, software tools, and network infrastructure.&nbsp;
Maintain demonstration equipment, test hardware, and supporting tools to ensure readiness for field use.
Assist with diagnosing and resolving technical issues during demonstration activities or system testing.&nbsp;
Provide hands-on support for RF systems, communication equipment, network connectivity, and hardware integration.&nbsp;
Coordinate with engineering teams to address system issues or performance anomalies discovered during demonstrations or testing.&nbsp;
Manage inventory, transport, and preparation of demonstration equipment used for customer engagements.&nbsp;
Ensure proper handling, packaging, and transport of sensitive technical equipment.&nbsp;
Support logistics planning for field deployments, including shipping, equipment preparation, and setup coordination.&nbsp;
Support Sales Consultants during technical discussions with customers by assisting with equipment setup and system operation.&nbsp;
Help demonstrate system functionality and capabilities during live customer demonstrations.&nbsp;
Assist in documenting demonstration results and gathering feedback to support future product improvements.&nbsp;
Work closely with engineering, operations, and business development teams to ensure demonstration environments accurately reflect product capabilities.&nbsp;
Provide feedback to engineering teams regarding demonstration performance, usability, and potential improvements.&nbsp;
Support internal testing and validation activities when demonstrations require integration with engineering prototypes or development systems.&nbsp;

JOB REQUIREMENTS AND MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS
Associate degree or technical certification in Electronics, Communications Technology, Telecommunications, or related field
A minimum of 5 years of industry experience in engineering, systems development, or program/project management roles within aerospace, space, or defense industries.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Experience managing cross-functional engineering and operations teams in complex technical programs.&nbsp;
Basic understanding of RF communications, satellite communications, or wireless communication systems.
Ability to set up and operate technical equipment used in communications demonstrations or testing environments.
Familiarity with antennas, ground station equipment, or network connectivity systems preferred.
Strong troubleshooting and hands-on technical problem-solving abilities.
Strong organizational and time management skills.
Ability to work collaboratively with both technical teams and customer-facing personnel.
PREFERRED EXPERIENCE
Proficiency in German and English (both written and spoken).&nbsp;&nbsp;
Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Knowledge of market analytics and technology planning and commercialization.
Experience with the aerospace telecommunications industry.&nbsp;
Experience with startups.&nbsp;
